FILED s521 (Fable, 2026-10-18 15:5x) from the CPAN-board failure review (docs/cpan-board-failure-review-s521.md Â§2c / Â§2d: Role-Tiny t/namespace-clean.t now LOADS its module (#3281 made B::Hooks::EndOfScope's prerequisite load) and dies at the READER: "too many colons in Class" -- the emission is `(p-delete-hash-slice %Local::Class:: @imports)`, a bare CL symbol with a trailing `::` that the reader rejects; the whole file is lost (4 perl rows).

Fable's re-probe on main c128e454 found the SILENT half (worse than the read error):

    package Local::Class; sub a { 1 } sub b { 2 } sub keep { 3 }
    package main; my @imports = qw(a b);
    delete @{"Local::Class::"}{@imports};
    print join(",", sort grep { defined &{"Local::Class::$_"} } qw(a b keep)), "\n";
perl 5.40.3: `keep`.   PCL: `a,b,keep` -- the delete ran, removed nothing, and nothing announced it.

TWO SHAPES, ONE MECHANISM: a stash reached as a hash (`%{"Pkg::"}`, `%Pkg::`, `$Pkg::{name}`, `delete`, `exists`, `keys`) -- the "Live symbol-table hashes" area that docs/not-supported.md marks DEFERRED (#1510 lists subs only; #3284).  Before fixing: grep DECIDED and not-supported for that ruling; the fix may be bounded to WRITES that remove a sub (delete of a stash element / slice = undefine the sub(s) + forget the glob, the CL side `fmakunbound` + the glob table) if the full live-hash model stays deferred -- a value-producing miss (`exists`, `keys`) must then DIE naming the deferral (rule 12), never answer wrong.  The READ ERROR shape: a package-qualified name with a trailing `::` used as a HASH must never be emitted as a bare symbol -- the emitter has a sibling for `%Foo::` (grep `_stash_hash` / `p-stash` in Pl/ExprToCL.pm); route the symbolic-string spelling through it.

ACCEPTANCE: the probe = perl (`keep`); Role-Tiny t/namespace-clean.t one-file run (4 rows; the `*FILE*` row leaves cpan-board14-fails.tsv by edit or is re-caused); a guard row (a Pl/t stash file -- grep `%main::` / `stash` in Pl/t), inverse-verified; the sweep (perl-tests/stash.t, op/stash.t companion one-file run) if cl/ changes.  Also an UNTIDY death today (a raw SBCL reader error banner) -- the USER's "fail tidily" rule applies independently.


=== DONE (s522b, commit f8408ef5 (rebased; was 15cffda3)) ===
Every stash-delete spelling reaches p-delete's write-through: p-delete-hash-slice routes a stash per key through p-delete; `@Pkg::{LIST}` lowers its container through the %Pkg:: stash arm (_bare_container_sym) -- no bare `%Pkg::` symbol.  A run-time lookup (defined &{"P::n"}, *{}{CODE}, dispatch) sees the sub gone; a COMPILED defined &P::n keeps it (perl's pinned glob; misc-fixes-02 row 23).  BAR: (a) keep, (b) clean transpile + keep; Fable's b2 probe 8 rows = perl; Role-Tiny namespace-clean.t runs 2/2 (NS:XS *FILE* row re-caused into rows 2 3 = #3632, nested BEGIN order); guard Pl/t/stash-hash-01.t.  AMENDED (s522b resumed s523, commit 8b28c226, Fable ruling s522 01:1x): a non-CODE element VALUE reads as its TYPEGLOB *Pkg::name (perl's own value -- the brief's "value dies" killed core Exporter's ${$pkg."::"}{EXPORT_FAIL} read in ten gate files); DELETING a non-CODE symbol dies `PCL: deleting a non-CODE symbol from a stash is not supported (docs/not-supported.md "Live symbol-table hashes")` (guard stash-hash-01 rule-12 row).  Interpolated "$Pkg::{x}" still reads "" -- #3635 (pre-existing).  COST OF THE RULED DELETE DEATH (measured s523): perl-tests/ref.t 200 (runperl `delete $::{x}`) and t/mro/basic.t rows 51 63 64 66 (`delete $Foo::{ISA}`), all passing before on a silent no-op; baselines edited row by row with the cause (0cbc74ea, 594d9aaf).  For Fable: perl's compiled $x keeps the pinned glob after the delete, so a no-op is right for compiled code and wrong only for symbolic lookups.  RE-RULED (Fable s523, after the cost measurement): the delete DEATH is WITHDRAWN -- deleting a non-CODE symbol is an EFFECT-ONLY miss (rule 12's s329 boundary), so it ANNOUNCES on stderr through %p-announce-unsupported ("PCL: stash delete: delete $Pkg::{name} of a non-CODE symbol is not implemented -- ignored (docs/not-supported.md "Live symbol-table hashes")") and continues, RETURNING THE DELETED GLOB (the snapshot holds it, so perl's return value is at hand, not undef); the sub-removal path is unchanged.  The variable stays in place -- perl's answer for compiled accesses; the stash-VIEW half (keys / exists / symbolic ${"Pkg::x"} see the symbol gone) is #3691.  Guard stash-hash-01 row 9 asserts the announcement + continuation (fails on the base, which is silent).  The rows that compare a child's stderr (perl-tests/ref.t 200, t/mro/basic.t 63 64 66) still fail on the announcement text alone; re-caused in the baselines.
